-- title:
--   Tame inertia in the Drinfeld identification at level field
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is a fixed algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$. Write $F :=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, that is, the subgroup of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; write `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, the subfield of the Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$ generated by the dilates `qExpand ℚ d jq` of the $q$-expansion of $j$ for $d \mid M'$; and for a field $\kappa$, `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the subfield of the Laurent series over $\kappa$ generated by the expansion of $j$ and by its $M'$-dilate.
--
--   (A) Base arithmetic data: a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `A.LiesOverPrime q`), whose residue field is written $\kappa$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ which, by `hW`, is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' κ` of places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` lies in `ssJSet q κ`; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into $F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, i.e. a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, tracing $A$ on the constants, compatible with the residue map of $A$ on constants, satisfying the scaling condition that every nonzero element has a constant multiple in `R₀.integers` with nonzero residue, and carrying a degree-preserving place map compatible with orders of functions; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which says that $R_0$ is coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a chosen element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   (B) The field of small constants: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; together with `hκ`: every element of $A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0 \cap A$.
--
--   (C) Auxiliary invariants: a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ whose image is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   (D) The layer family: an index type, a family $K$ of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ induced by $A$ (`hAn`), an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0} \le K_n$ for all $n$, and the cofinality hypothesis `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is contained in the image of some $K_n$.
--
--   (E) The tame parameter and stability: an element $\pi_t \in A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q$; the hypothesis `htame`, that every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$) with `A.tameCharacter πt τ` $=1$ fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise, where `A.tameCharacter π τ` is the residue of $\tau(\pi)/\pi$ in $\kappa$ when that quotient lies in $A$, and $0$ otherwise; and `hk₀stab`, that every $\mathbb Q$-automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ preserving $A$ maps $k_0$ into $k_0$.
--
--   (F) The constant valuation ring: an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ induced by $A$ (`hAb`), and a nonzero generator $\varpi_b$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The field $F$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is then about every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ subject to the following conditions.
--
--   The conditions on $F_0$ are: (F1) an element $f$ of $F$ lies in $F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$; (F2) the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $F$; (F3) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (F4) linear disjointness: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   The conditions on $W_0$ form the level-field model package, whose clauses are: (W1) for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$; (W2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; (W3) the maximal ideal of $W_0$ is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; (W4) specialisation at $s$: for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` and which is regular wherever $j$ is (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$), if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $g$ in $F$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals `s.evalAt` of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; (W5) for all $\zeta$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, membership in $W_0$ is unchanged by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` on elements of $F_0$ whose image again lies in $F_0$; (W6) existence of an affine chart: there are a subring $B$ of $F$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that the structure map is the inclusion of constants; $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of that compositum is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the quotient of $B$ by $\varpi_b$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ consists exactly of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$; the image of $j$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; there is an element of $B \cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that traces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$, and at which no monic polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients evaluated at $j$ falls in the maximal ideal of $V$; for each $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there is an element of $B \cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring of $F_0$ that traces $A$ and satisfies the analogue of (W4) at $s'$; two Drinfeld-reduction clauses, asserting for each $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ (respectively for each ring homomorphism $\mathbb F_{q^2} \to \kappa$), under the hypothesis that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, the existence of a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ of cardinality $2\,$`placeWidthChar q M' s` and of homomorphisms $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with kernel the ideal generated by $\varpi_b$, prescribed on constants, with all of the target a ratio of $\rho$-values, with image characterised by the image of [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), intertwining the level automorphisms with [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma, 1)$, and in the second clause also intertwining the arithmetic action of tame inertia with the action at $(\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^q)^{-1}), \alpha^q)$; and a final clause producing $q+1$ node subrings of $F_0$ together with the accompanying structure, namely integrality of $j$ for $R_0$ at $s$, membership of [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) in $F$, a constant $a_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue has $q$-th power equal to the value of the residue of $j$ at $s$ (the Hasse relation), a common subring presenting all nodes as localisations, transitive permutation of the nodes by the level automorphisms, mutual distinctness, the dichotomy that every valuation subring of $F_0$ tracing $A$ and centred at $s$ either contains $B$ or dominates a node, and, for each node $O$, that $O$ is contained in $W_0$, is local and noetherian, traces $A$ on constants, has all residues constant, and admits an exponent $E_0 \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,w(s)}v$ for a unit $v$ of $k_0 \cap A$, branch parameters $c_x,c_y$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^{E_0}u$, an isomorphism of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the completion of $A \cap k_0$ at $\pi_0^{E_0}$ carrying constants to constants and $c_x,c_y$ to unit multiples of $U$ and $V$, the statement that $c_y$ is in and $c_x$ is outside the maximal ideal of $W_0$, an Igusa datum expressing `jqNModC` minus $a_0$ as a unit times a positive power of $V$, a branch valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with its own list of properties (domination of $O$, tracing of $A$, discreteness, uniformiser $\pi_0$, a residually transcendental element, interchange of the roles of $c_x$ and $c_y$, a chart description of reductions of functions, and separation from the other nodes), and a chart subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ with its own list of properties (containment in $B$ and in $O$, a pole condition relative to $j$, presentation of $O$ as a localisation of $B_x$, generation of $F_0$ by fractions, finite generation over the $A$-integral constants, and a witness avoiding suitable valuation subrings). These clauses are summarised here; each is a hypothesis of the theorem.
--
--   Under all of this, the conclusion is the following. Let `FSS` be any field which is an algebra over $\kappa$ and let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ from $F$ to `FSS`, that is, a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ with a surjective residue homomorphism `R.residue` onto `FSS` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, tracing $A$ on the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, compatible with the residue map of $A$ on constants, and such that every nonzero element of $F$ has a constant multiple in `R.integers` with nonzero residue; assume that $R$ traces $W_0$ on $F_0$, i.e. for every $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in$ `R.integers` if and only if $f \in W_0$. Then for every ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb F_{q^2} \to \kappa$, with $\kappa$ regarded as an $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra through $\iota$, and under the hypothesis that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, there is a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ with $$\#C_s = 2\,\mathtt{placeWidthChar}\ q\ M'\ s,$$ where `placeWidthChar q M' s` is `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of $s$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`, such that for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` there is an isomorphism of $\kappa$-algebras $e$ from `FSS` onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the actions of the pairs $(1,\zeta')$ with $\zeta' \in C_s$, with the following two properties.
--
--   First, equivariance for the level action: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, given that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers` and that the pair (`redQ q γ`, $1$) lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(\gamma,\beta) \mapsto \det(\gamma)\beta^{q+1}$), one has, for every $x$ in `FSS`, that $e$ applied to the residual automorphism `R.resAut` of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` at $x$ equals [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at (`redQ q γ`, $1$) applied to $e(x)$, the equality being taken in the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   Second, equivariance for tame inertia: for every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, every $\alpha \in \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $\iota(\alpha) =$ `A.tameCharacter πt τ`, and every semilinear automorphism $g$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ equal to [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) (the coefficientwise action of $\tau$), it holds that $g$ preserves `R.integers`, i.e. $g \cdot f \in$ `R.integers` if and only if $f \in$ `R.integers`; and, for any witness of this stability and any ring automorphism $\varphi$ of `FSS` inducing the reduction of $g$, in the sense that `R.residue` of $g \cdot f$ equals $\varphi$ of `R.residue` of $f$ for all $f$ in `R.integers`, and for every $d \in (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ equals $\alpha^{q+1}$ and for which the pair (`diagOneElem q (d ^ q)⁻¹`, $\alpha^q$), with `diagOneElem q u` the matrix $\mathrm{diag}(1,u)$, lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), one has, for every $x$ in `FSS`, that $e(\varphi(x))$ equals [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at that pair applied to $e(x)$, again as an identity in the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   This is the tame-inertia form of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) description of a supersingular residue disc on the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with level group the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$: the residual field of any prolongation of $A$ tracing the level-field valuation ring $W_0$ is identified with the $C_s$-fixed subfield of the Drinfeld function field over $\kappa$, compatibly with the $\Gamma_0(M')$-action and with the arithmetic action of the inertia group of $A$ through the tame character at $\pi_t$. It is the input consumed by the packaged existence theorem [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart), which assembles the semistable model data at $q$ used in the level-lowering argument.
